From 787c2bef8fbe5b13540440c4ac3b1d76d45332d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cindy Krafft <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:49:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Give a sampled domain's first residue its null2 ratio in
 region_trace_ensemble()

In region_trace_ensemble() the loop that adds 1.0 for residues outside
a sampled domain ran up to and including tr->sqfrom[d], the first
M-emitted residue of the domain, so that residue was counted as
outside (odds 1.0) instead of with the domain's null2 odds in every
sampled trace. The comments and p7_trace_Index() define the domain as
sqfrom..sqto inclusive.

This changes the per-residue null2 scores of every region resolved by
stochastic traceback clustering. Re-deriving those scores from the same
200 sampled traces for 25 human fn3-containing proteins, the library's
n2sc matches the loop as written at 2356/2356 residues and the
documented rule at 1444/2356 (max difference 0.29 nats); with this
change it matches the documented rule.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TaHntBDKuZJpMAAMenkC44
---
 src/p7_domaindef.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/p7_domaindef.c b/src/p7_domaindef.c
index 5d61e616..7b859c53 100644
--- a/src/p7_domaindef.c
+++ b/src/p7_domaindef.c
@@ -625,7 +625,7 @@ region_trace_ensemble(P7_DOMAINDEF *ddef, const P7_OPROFILE *om, const ESL_DSQ *
 	  p7_Null2_ByTrace(om, ddef->tr, ddef->tr->tfrom[d], ddef->tr->tto[d], wrk, null2);
 	  
 	  /* residues outside domains get bumped +1: because f'(x) = f(x), so f'(x)/f(x) = 1 in these segments */
-	  for (; pos <= ddef->tr->sqfrom[d]; pos++) ddef->n2sc[ireg+pos-1] += 1.0;
+	  for (; pos <  ddef->tr->sqfrom[d]; pos++) ddef->n2sc[ireg+pos-1] += 1.0;
 
 	  /* Residues inside domains get bumped by their null2 ratio */
 	  for (; pos <= ddef->tr->sqto[d];   pos++) ddef->n2sc[ireg+pos-1] += null2[dsq[ireg+pos-1]];
